text:
A rule~$R$,
\[
\AxiomC{$S_1$}
\AxiomC{$\dots$}
\AxiomC{$S_n$}
\RightLabel{$R$}
\TrinaryInfC{$S$}
\DisplayProof
\]
is \emph{!!{height}-preserving admissible} (or
\emph{!!{hp}-admissible}) in a system if, whenever $\Proves[h_i] S_i$
for $i = 1$, \dots,~$n$, then $\Proves_m S$ with $m = \max(h_1, \dots,
h_n)$.
